From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:16:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] serial: core: shut down a closed port when its console is
 detached

A port that was opened and closed while it was the console keeps
tty_port_initialized() set, because tty_port_shutdown() returns early
for console ports. Detaching the console then left it powered: the
power-off on detach only covered a port that had never been
initialized, and nothing else shut it down, so on MediaTek 8250 one
runtime PM reference stayed and kept the UART's bus clock on.

On detach, if no one has the port open, run the shutdown the earlier
close skipped, which also powers the port off; power off a port that
was never initialized as before.
---
 drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
index 81f78890b..f8661d8dd 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
@@ -2981,8 +2981,19 @@ static ssize_t console_store(struct device *dev,
 		 * power it off now if nobody has it open, as for any other port.
 		 */
 		port->console = false;
-		if (!tty_port_initialized(port))
-			uart_change_pm(state, UART_PM_STATE_OFF);
+		if (!tty_port_active(port)) {
+			/*
+			 * A close while it was the console skipped the shutdown
+			 * and left the port initialized; do that shutdown now,
+			 * which also powers it off.
+			 */
+			if (tty_port_initialized(port)) {
+				tty_port_set_initialized(port, false);
+				port->ops->shutdown(port);
+			} else {
+				uart_change_pm(state, UART_PM_STATE_OFF);
+			}
+		}
 	} else if (!oldconsole && newconsole) {
 		if (!uart_console(uport))
 			return -ENOENT;
